																		Author&#039;s Post - When I&#039;m gaming I tend to forget about sleeping. Sometimes I even forget to breathe.
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/decibelles" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2005044); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2005044&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606250283" alt="Decibelles" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2005044)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/decibelles" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2005044); return false;" >Decibelles</a></span> <span class="odate time_1496603325 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">04 Jun 2017 19:08</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2841799">
									

<p>Thanks to the following people:</p>
<ul>
<li><span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/th4nkyoub3n" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3079214); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3079214&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1506814055" alt="th4nkyoub3n" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3079214)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/th4nkyoub3n" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3079214); return false;">th4nkyoub3n</a></span> for writing the original (which had very very good ideas and concepts) and working on this rewrite with me. He is my co-author.</li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li><span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/roget" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1229263); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1229263&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1506814055" alt="Roget" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1229263)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/roget" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1229263); return false;">Roget</a></span>, <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/taffeta" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2221240); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2221240&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1506814055" alt="Taffeta" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2221240)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/taffeta" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2221240); return false;">Taffeta</a></span>, and <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/a-random-day" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1841781); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1841781&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1506814055" alt="A Random Day" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1841781)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/a-random-day" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1841781); return false;">A Random Day</a></span> for tone and phrasing stuff.</li>
<li><span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/kinchtheknifeblade" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1345012); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1345012&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1506814055" alt="kinchtheknifeblade" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1345012)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/kinchtheknifeblade" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1345012); return false;">kinchtheknifeblade</a></span> for backstory stuff that helped me out with this a bit.</li>
<li><span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/dolphinslugchugger" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1969477); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1969477&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1506814055" alt="DolphinSlugchugger" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1969477)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/dolphinslugchugger" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1969477); return false;">DolphinSlugchugger</a></span> for general feedback.</li>
<li>The SomethingAwful SCP thread. Not for helping me with this, but because I read about 75 pages of it on a binge one night and was amused and entertained by both their good and bad opinions.</li>
</ul>
<p>If I forgot anyone else, lemme know! The original can be found <a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20170526162613/http://scp-wiki.net/scp-3054">here</a>.</p>
<p>Stuff that's canon that I had no way of incorporating naturally into the article:</p>
<ol>
<li>She speaks in a metallic-sounding voice.</li>
<li>Her &quot;moms&quot; are Dahlia and Andressa, aka hetcopogg and gaycopmp4.</li>
<li>The redaction contains scientific technobabble related to the pink blood (so to speak) and its similarities to real blood and oil, which I didn't wanna include cause it clashes with the tone of this article. You need to be Level 3 and above in order to see that stuff, or working on 890's team.</li>
<li>It respawns at that GameStop. Her moms picked her up.</li>
<li>Heather is a reference to Heather Mason. You know the reference.</li>
</ol>
<p>Author questions:</p>
<ol>
<li>Are you a true gamer?</li>
<li>What sort of person do you think SCP-3090 was in her old life, before becoming a MAW?</li>
<li>How do you think Dahlia helped out with the creation of SCP-3090?</li>
</ol>
<p>What I Listened to While Writing: A lot, actually. So how about this skip's unofficial <a href="https://homestuck.bandcamp.com/track/gamegrl-original-1993-mix">theme song</a>?</p>
<hr />
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Ported&nbsp;from&nbsp;my&nbsp;author&nbsp;page&nbsp;discussion&nbsp;thread.</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>This is my best writing on the site simply because it expresses a lot of what I want to tell about the Foundation in a simple, streamlined way. The interactions between humanoid anomaly and researcher, the line of treating the anomaly like an object versus a person, mental health, video games, being gay, being trans, etc.. I could (and absolutely can) write an entire article on each of these subjects alone, but figured each of them can make an interesting part of a whole story in one article. Mental health is a big thing for me, something I'm both hurt by and fascinated by. How does one react under certain situations? The whole mantra of showing and not telling applies here, but I wanted to tell a bit to get it across. Heather escapes in video games in a sort of real literal sense, while alive and while an anomaly. It's a good way to escape anxiety and depression, and I feel much the same way.</p>
<p>Plus, any article people will cite it as an example of the SCP Wiki failing, being shitty as a whole merely by existing, being too SJW, or act like immature babies over is a real successful one. It weeds out the people who read fiction for the wrong reasons and don't want to look closer into. Plus, I feel like I've succeeded in creating a character I genuinely love with this. I've never written a character before that I was really into, either merely liking or writing only in service to the story. So, yeah, this is my favorite thing of mine and maybe the best thing I've written.</p>
<p>There's also a contingent of people who hate this solely because it has any association with Gamers Against Weed, to which I say, come the fuck on. The main thrust and core of this article only uses that as a launchpad to run with something else altogether. Anyone who read this, saw the GoI, and downvoted never had an interest in connecting to or reading or analyzing this article on any sort of scale IMO. It'd almost be entirely the same without the GAW connection. The only major things I'd lose are the sense of community and the theme of minorities carving their way out in the world of anomalous happenings, both of which I think provide necessary background to make this more than &quot;cute girl with TV for head does stuff to video games&quot;. It adds a layer to this that makes it more human. I will admit that not every reader is gonna be connected to someone who's trans and gay and is a girl, and who has a defensive guard surrounding that to dictate their actions. But also, nearly everything I write on this site now is filled with LGBT themes, so it's just par for the course if you're reading my stuff.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

