			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2843076">
									

<p>Dahlia and Andressa asked chat if they could make Mr. MAVG a girl instead. Everyone was fine with it. They made it. This was after some of the Misters<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-390072-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-390072-1')">1</a></sup> had already been made. Regardless of what the other lists said, GAW was fine with it, and so it came to be.</p>
<p>If someone wanted to write Ms. Zapatista as a male, well, they could, and they could technically use the same reasoning as above, but it sort of ties into how popular media and culture doesn't have nearly as many girls as it does boys, with how severely underrepresented they are. That's why I made a Mr. a Ms.; because I thought there could be more female representation as far as the series list went. It's more deep than the creators in-universe gave it, because I want to make my writings more representative and less &quot;white cishet guy&quot; (she's obviously none of those) than what sci-fi/horror/fantasy writing usually comprises of. So, if you wanted to make Ms. Zapatista Mr. Zapatista, there should be a good reason for it.</p>
