														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2843244">
									

<p>I think MAVG's new gender suits her better. The only reason I didn't consider it before was because I didn't feel comfortable taking too many liberties with things that were previously established.</p>
<p>Similar to how only Mr. Hax's list has the Humble Waterfilter Merchant and how that can't be added to existing articles without permission of the original authors, I don't want other people to edit current lists to change Mr. to Ms. unless they are the authors of the articles. Did jockjamsvol6, creator of Mr. Bernie Sanders, left GAW before Ms. MAVG was finalized? I don't know. I don't feel like it's my choice to make. I just know that the list Mr. Ominous made had it as Mr. Mad About Video Games</p>
<p>I did change the list on Mr. Literal Serial Killer, however. None of the names on that list matched the original in the first place so I felt like that list was beyond such a restriction.</p>
<p>This is just me speaking about my own gender headcanons at this point, but I feel that Mr. Deadly Sins does not identify as any sort of gender and presents as whatever the community would find &quot;trustworthy.&quot; Mr. Deadly Sins male assignment is superficial in nature.</p>

